# TCP Qubic Client (TODO)

The "real" Qubic client speaks a custom binary TCP protocol to a
running Qubic node. We don't ship it yet because:

1. It requires a running Qubic node (or access to one)
2. The binary protocol is detailed in the Qubic source and varies
   between network versions
3. Most local dev + CI workflows are happy with the stub

## When you implement this

```ts
// src/client/tcp.ts
import * as net from "node:net";
import { QubicClient, ... } from "./types.js";

export class TcpQubicClient implements QubicClient {
  constructor(private opts: { host: string; port: number }) {}

  private send<T>(payload: Buffer): Promise<T> {
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const socket = net.connect(this.opts.port, this.opts.host);
      // ... write payload, read response, parse
    });
  }

  async ping() { /* ... */ }
  async getCurrentTick() { /* ... */ }
  // ...
}
```

## Protocol notes (from the Qubic source)

- Each request has an 8-byte header: `[type: u32][size: u32][payload: bytes]`
- Common request types: `BROADCAST_TRANSACTION` (0x10), `GET_CURRENT_TICK_INFO` (0x14), `GET_BALANCE` (0x18), `GET_TRANSACTIONS_BY_ADDRESS` (0x42)
- Responses have a similar 8-byte header followed by a typed payload
- The signature scheme is K12-based (see `services/identity/src/lib/qubic.ts` for context)

## References

- https://github.com/qubic/core (Qubic core implementation in C++)
- https://docs.qubic.org/ (when it exists)
- qubic-js (community TypeScript SDK, when it ships)

Once this lands, add it to the factory in `client/index.ts`.
